WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.144 --> 00:00:02.828
Hi, I'm Beth Engstrom.

2
00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:05.828
My father, Walter, is a patient at
Kestrel Falls Community Hospital,

3
00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:07.661
and he talked with Laura Hemmingsen too.

4
00:00:07.661 --> 00:00:11.092
Laura asked me how I help him with his
care, so let me explain.

5
00:00:11.092 --> 00:00:14.354
Dad's doing well, but he's seventy-eight and
he has a lot of appointments,

6
00:00:14.354 --> 00:00:16.601
and I live about an hour away.

7
00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:20.823
I'm the one who keeps his pill list up to date
and reminds him about his visits.

8
00:00:20.823 --> 00:00:22.320
I go with him to the heart
doctor when I can,

9
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.626
and I call the clinic when
something's unclear.

10
00:00:24.626 --> 00:00:31.229
Right now, the only way I can see anything is to
log in as Dad, with his password.

11
00:00:31.229 --> 00:00:32.413
I know that's not how it's
supposed to work,

12
00:00:32.413 --> 00:00:37.446
but the old portal didn't give me another
way that I could figure out,

13
00:00:37.446 --> 00:00:39.656
and calling the clinic means
sitting on hold.

14
00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:43.694
So I log in as him, I check his
appointments, and I read his messages.

15
00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:45.777
Sometimes I answer them as him,
which I know isn't great.

16
00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:49.040
Here's why that's a problem.

17
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.744
When I message the nurse, she
thinks it's Dad.

18
00:00:51.744 --> 00:00:55.674
If she asks a question, she might think he
understood it when it was really me.

19
00:00:55.674 --> 00:00:58.226
And I can see things he might
not want me to see.

20
00:00:58.226 --> 00:01:00.636
I try not to look, but it's
all just there.

21
00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:03.021
So I'm actually hopeful about
the new system.

22
00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:05.962
What I need is my own login,
as his helper,

23
00:01:05.962 --> 00:01:10.074
so I can see his appointments and his
medication list and message his nurse.

24
00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:12.170
Proxy access, I think they call it.

25
00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.561
And a clear phone number or contact for
when something goes wrong.

26
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:18.997
To make the setup easy, make it
something I can do once, with Dad,

27
00:01:18.997 --> 00:01:21.304
maybe at his next appointment, instead of
mailing forms back and forth.

28
00:01:21.304 --> 00:01:23.595
Let him choose what I can see.

29
00:01:23.595 --> 00:01:28.228
And give me a way to show I'm his
helper when I call,

30
00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:28.828
so the front desk doesn't have to guess.

31
00:01:28.228 --> 00:01:32.876
My fear is that I won't be
able to help him.

32
00:01:32.876 --> 00:01:35.957
That something changes in his
medicines and nobody tells me,

33
00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:40.004
or that the new system locks me out and I don't
find out until he misses something.

34
00:01:40.004 --> 00:01:44.509
During the switch, I'd want to know ahead of
time: will his appointments carry

35
00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:47.103
over, will his refills still go
to the same pharmacy,

36
00:01:47.103 --> 00:01:48.898
and who do I call if they don't?

37
00:01:48.898 --> 00:01:50.880
I don't want to read
everything, by the way.

38
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.612
Just what I need to help him.

39
00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.647
Dad has some things that are
his, and that's fine.

40
00:01:55.647 --> 00:02:00.362
I'd actually feel better if the
system kept those separate,

41
00:02:00.362 --> 00:02:00.962
so I'm not seeing them by accident.

42
00:02:00.362 --> 00:02:05.529
How would I want to hear about the switch
and what it means for Dad?

43
00:02:05.529 --> 00:02:07.791
Email or a text, honestly.

44
00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:09.755
I'm busy, I work full time, and I'm
driving to Dad's on weekends.

45
00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:13.559
A short message with the date, what's
changing, and what I need to do.

46
00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:15.597
Then a reminder a week before.

47
00:02:15.597 --> 00:02:19.125
And if there's a help line for families,
put the number at the top,

48
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:20.387
not buried at the bottom.

49
00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:24.849
I've talked with a few friends who
take care of their parents.

50
00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:26.626
Most of them do what I do, log in
as their mom or dad.

51
00:02:26.626 --> 00:02:31.962
One of them got locked out after she guessed
the password wrong too many times,

52
00:02:31.962 --> 00:02:33.306
and her mom missed a refill.

53
00:02:33.306 --> 00:02:33.906
So it's not just me.

54
00:02:33.306 --> 00:02:36.675
If you make proxy access easy, you'll
help a lot of families.

55
00:02:36.675 --> 00:02:41.442
And if you want someone to try the proxy
setup early and give feedback,

56
00:02:41.442 --> 00:02:42.042
I'd absolutely do it.

57
00:02:41.442 --> 00:02:44.345
I'd be a good tester.

58
00:02:44.345 --> 00:02:47.360
I'm pretty good with computers, and I know
exactly what's confusing now.

